{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784633136,"nonce":"oy3Ab6Gq77LcEfCX3SwDtUKNFl0=","title":"Service containers need a run-as-root opt-in (stock DB images fail runAsNonRoot)","message":"ADR-0058 says run-as-root is the expected self-service grant for stock DB images (official postgres starts as root to fix perms). But ServiceSpec (sidecar) and SharedServiceSpec have no security/run_as_root field, so a service container inherits only the host step's setting (sidecar) or runs non-root unconditionally (shared). Result: a stock postgres shared service fails under the ADR-0039 restricted baseline (runAsNonRoot). Add a self-service run_as_root opt-in on the service specs (and later the digest-keyed governed add-caps/privileged). Surfaced writing .scarab/dogfood.yaml. Would bite on the first live-cluster dogfood.","files":null}]}